module

public import Sheaf.AlgebraicGeometry.ToriMultiplicativeType
public import WeilConjectures.AlgebraicGeometry.SchemeTangentSpace
public import Mathlib.CategoryTheory.Monoidal.Cartesian.Mod
public import Mathlib.AlgebraicGeometry.Morphisms.FiniteType
import Sheaf.AlgebraicGeometry.TorusFixedLocalIdealJets
import Sheaf.AlgebraicGeometry.RationalTangentCotangentDuality
import Sheaf.AlgebraicGeometry.GmRepresentationWeightBasis
import Mathlib.RingTheory.Filtration
import WeilConjectures.AlgebraicGeometry.GroupScheme.Defs

/-! # A torus action on a connected group is detected on its tangent space

Source: Conrad, Reductive Group Schemes, Proposition 3.3.8, proof on printed p.102,
citing CGP, Corollary A.8.11
(blueprint: lem-sfb-torus-action-connected-group-lie-rigidity).

The differential is expressed by its defining dual-number formula, after every
commutative algebra extension. A vector at the identity over B is a B[epsilon]-point
reducing to the identity. The acting point is pulled back from B, so the formula
expresses the whole tangent representation, including over nonreduced algebras.
-/

@[expose] public section

set_option autoImplicit false

universe u

open CategoryTheory CartesianMonoidalCategory Opposite
open scoped MonObj

namespace AlgebraicGeometry

/-- An action by group automorphisms of a split torus on a connected affine
finite-type group scheme is trivial exactly when its full tangent representation is.
The right side is the dual-number definition of the differential: lift t along
B -> B[epsilon], act on a point theta reducing to the identity, and require theta
itself. This is identity on all vectors, hence identity of the induced linear maps.
No smoothness or reducedness hypothesis is imposed.

Source: Conrad, Reductive Group Schemes, Proposition 3.3.8, printed p.102,
and CGP, Corollary A.8.11
(blueprint: lem-sfb-torus-action-connected-group-lie-rigidity).

Proof:
1. By lem-sfb-universal-fixed-subscheme the fixed functor is a closed subscheme F.
   Affineness implies separatedness. Its points form subgroups after every algebra
   extension, so F is a closed subgroup containing the identity. Put R = O_(H,e),
   with maximal ideal m. By lem-sfb-rational-point-thickenings-base-change, R is
   Noetherian local with residue k. By lem-sfb-torus-fixed-local-ideal-jets the
   identity stalk of F is R/J, with J generated by t*f-f, and the finite jet
   algebras and their maximal ideals carry rational torus representations.
2. By lem-sc-rational-tangent-cotangent-duality the trivial tangent action implies
   triviality on m/m^2: finite-dimensional dual functionals separate vectors.
3. Apply lem-sfb-gm-representation-weight-basis to each commuting torus factor.
   Every weight on m/m^2 is zero, since a nonzero Laurent character is nontrivial
   on some k-point. In each m/m^(n+1), lift a cotangent basis using weight-zero
   components. Successively replacing factors modulo higher powers of m shows
   these lifts generate R/m^(n+1) as an algebra. Thus every jet action is trivial.
   This also covers a zero-dimensional cotangent space and a rank-zero torus.
4. All differences generating J lie in every power of m. Apply
   lem-weil-pbc-krull-intersection-jacobson to the cyclic R-module R to get J=0.
   Therefore the actual identity-stalk map for F -> H is an isomorphism.
5. By lem-sfb-closed-subgroup-identity-stalk-detection, the closed subgroup F is
   H. The restricted-action clause of lem-sfb-universal-fixed-subscheme says
   that the action morphism is the projection, on all algebra-valued points.
6. Conversely the projection acts identically on every dual-number vector after
   every algebra extension, precisely the defining tangent-map formula in
   def-sc-scheme-tangent-space. -/
theorem torus_action_connected_group_iff_tangent_trivial
    {k : Type u} [Field k] [IsAlgClosed k]
    (H : Over (Spec (.of k))) [GrpObj H] [IsAffine H.left]
    [ConnectedSpace H.left] [LocallyOfFiniteType H.hom] [QuasiCompact H.hom]
    (T : Grp (Over (Spec (.of k)))) (r : ℕ)
    (hT : Nonempty (T ≅ MultiplicativeType.splitTorus k r))
    [ModObj T.X H]
    (hgroup : ∀ (B : CommAlgCat.{u} k)
      (t : (algSpec (.of k)).obj (op B) ⟶ T.X)
      (h h' : (algSpec (.of k)).obj (op B) ⟶ H),
      t • (h * h') = (t • h) * (t • h')) :
    γ[T.X, H] = snd T.X H ↔
      ∀ (B : CommAlgCat.{u} k)
        (t : (algSpec (.of k)).obj (op B) ⟶ T.X)
        (θ : (algSpec (.of k)).obj (op (CommAlgCat.of k (DualNumber B))) ⟶ H),
        (algSpec (.of k)).map (CommAlgCat.ofHom (TrivSqZeroExt.fstHom k B B)).op ≫ θ = 1 →
        ((algSpec (.of k)).map (CommAlgCat.ofHom (TrivSqZeroExt.inlAlgHom k B B)).op ≫ t) •
          θ = θ := by
  sorry

end AlgebraicGeometry
